1
00:00:02,910 --> 00:00:04,160
- Hi.     - Hey.

2
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:06,630
So, uh, did everything go okay with the annulment?

3
00:00:06,790 --> 00:00:09,290
Oh, yeah. No problems. It's all taken care of.

4
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:10,800
- Ross, thank you.     - Ah.

5
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:15,220
- You guys want to go see a movie?     - Yeah, why not?

6
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:17,590
- Let me get my sweater.     - Okay.

7
00:00:20,310 --> 00:00:21,890
Want to hear something weird?

8
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:23,390
Always.

9
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:27,150
I didn't get the annulment.

10
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:31,110
- What?     - We're still married.

11
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:34,530
Don't tell Rachel. See you later.

12
00:00:38,030 --> 00:00:41,660
- Hey, do you have any gum?     - Oh, yeah.

13
00:00:41,830 --> 00:00:45,870
Wait! Wait! Hi. Ross, can I just talk to you for just a second?

14
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:47,880
Oh, but we'll be late for the movie.

15
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,500
Oh, there's a cab. Taxi!

16
00:00:50,670 --> 00:00:52,170
Oh, that's great.

17
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:55,010
What timing! My God, huh? There you go.

18
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:58,470
We're gonna walk. It's right at the Angelika.

19
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:00,050
Oh, the Angelika! Go! Go!

20
00:01:02,350 --> 00:01:04,100
You didn't get the annulment?

21
00:01:04,310 --> 00:01:07,440
- I know.     - Ross!

22
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:10,940
I tried, but when I got to my lawyer's office, all I heard was:

23
00:01:11,150 --> 00:01:13,690
"Three divorces! Three divorces!"

24
00:01:15,110 --> 00:01:19,660
I just don't want my tombstone to read "Ross Geller: Three Divorces."

25
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:23,410
Don't worry about that. Your tombstone can say whatever you want.

26
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:26,410
It can say, "Ross Geller: Good at Marriage."

27
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:31,790
You know? Mine's gonna say, "Phoebe Buffay: Buried Alive."

28
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:35,880
All I know is, I can't have another failed marriage.

29
00:01:36,090 --> 00:01:39,970
So you're gonna be married to a girl who doesn't even know about it?

30
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:42,010
Woman. Sorry.

31
00:01:43,430 --> 00:01:47,060
Well, okay, so I don't have it all worked out quite yet.

32
00:01:47,310 --> 00:01:52,860
- Just don't say anything to Rachel.     - Rachel is one of my closest friends.

33
00:01:53,150 --> 00:01:57,360
But being the only one that knows about this makes me feel special. Okay.

34
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:02,830
Okay, stop, stop! Phoebe?

35
00:02:02,990 --> 00:02:04,370
Hey, Rach!

36
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:07,120
What was that?

37
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:08,960
Sorry. Mix-up.

38
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,330
How was the movie?

39
00:02:12,130 --> 00:02:13,960
I haven't seen it yet.

40
00:02:14,210 --> 00:02:16,380
You'd better hurry. The Angelika! Go. Go!

41
00:02:16,550 --> 00:02:18,010
No!

42
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000

43
00:02:59,630 --> 00:03:02,260
When we move in together, can I get a gumball machine?

44
00:03:02,430 --> 00:03:05,390
Of course. Joey wouldn't let you have one?

45
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:08,810
No, when it comes to sweets, he's surprisingly strict.

46
00:03:09,810 --> 00:03:11,940
Did you tell him you're moving out?

47
00:03:12,190 --> 00:03:15,480
No, I keep trying. And I can get out "Joey, I have to..."

48
00:03:15,730 --> 00:03:19,650
Then I lose my nerve and I finish with "...go to the bathroom."

49
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:21,820
He may think I'm sick.

50
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:26,160
I have to tell Rachel, but I... We just gotta get it over with.

51
00:03:26,410 --> 00:03:29,660
Next time we see them, we'll just tell them. That's it.

52
00:03:29,870 --> 00:03:33,040
That's how it'll work now? You'll just order me around?

53
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,710
- Pretty much.     - All right.

54
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:39,000
Hey, Monica. Hey, man, you feeling better?

55
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:44,470
Joey.

56
00:03:44,890 --> 00:03:46,600
We have something to tell you.

57
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:48,890
Oh, my God!

58
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:50,850
You're pregnant!

59
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:54,600
No! No?

60
00:03:54,770 --> 00:03:56,440
- No.     - No!

61
00:03:57,860 --> 00:04:00,150
Look, Joe, here's the thing. Um...

62
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:05,570
Monica and I have decided to live together, here.

63
00:04:06,450 --> 00:04:08,450
So I'm gonna be moving out, man.

64
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:13,500
Wow.

65
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:15,580
Oh, uh, hey!

66
00:04:15,790 --> 00:04:19,960
I'm really happy for you guys. Congratulations. See you later.

67
00:04:20,170 --> 00:04:22,090
- Joey! Joey! Are you okay?     - Yeah.

68
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:24,760
I gotta go. I've got an acting job.

69
00:04:26,930 --> 00:04:28,180
Like you'd believe that.

70
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:31,220
This sucks!

71
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:34,350
I'll be across the hall. And I promise you...

72
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:38,110
the minute Monica and I break up, I'm moving right back in.

73
00:04:39,650 --> 00:04:41,860
Look, uh, If you're gonna move in with him...

74
00:04:42,030 --> 00:04:45,320
I feel it is my responsibility to tell you the truth about him.

75
00:04:45,490 --> 00:04:47,610
He's a terrible roommate. Terrible.

76
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:49,530
He, uh, forgets to, um...

77
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:53,160
He always, he always, uh...

78
00:04:53,910 --> 00:04:55,910
Who am I kidding? He's the best roommate!

79
00:05:01,550 --> 00:05:04,010
- Hey, Pheebs. Have you seen Rachel?     - Hey.

80
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:06,430
- No, why?     - I have some exciting news.

81
00:05:06,970 --> 00:05:08,140
You're pregnant.

82
00:05:09,470 --> 00:05:11,010
No!

83
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:13,930
Chandler and I are moving in together.

84
00:05:14,140 --> 00:05:15,680
Oh, that's good!

85
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:19,560
But if you were pregnant, what would you name it? Hint, Phoebe.

86
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:23,150
- Hey.     - Hey.

87
00:05:23,530 --> 00:05:25,400
- What's up?     - Well, um...

88
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:29,200
Chandler and I are moving in together.

89
00:05:29,450 --> 00:05:31,580
Oh, my God.

90
00:05:31,910 --> 00:05:35,450
Oh, my little sister and my best friend...

91
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:37,290
shacking up.

92
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,840
That's great. That's great. Mwah.

93
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,050
- Guys, I'm happy too.     - Okay, come here.

94
00:05:46,130 --> 00:05:50,680
Big day, huh? People moving in. People getting annulled.

95
00:05:53,850 --> 00:05:55,720
I gotta go find Rachel. But, um...

96
00:05:55,980 --> 00:06:00,270
If you see her, give her some really bad news, so mine doesn't seem so bad.

97
00:06:00,730 --> 00:06:02,150
Okay, bye.

98
00:06:03,150 --> 00:06:06,070
Hmm. Something bad to tell Rachel.

99
00:06:07,650 --> 00:06:10,280
Bad news for Rachel. What could that be?

100
00:06:11,530 --> 00:06:13,830
Can you just lay off, please?

101
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:18,620
My life is an embarrassment. I should just go live under somebody's stairs.

102
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:22,920
It's not that big a deal. You'll have been divorced three times.

103
00:06:23,170 --> 00:06:25,210
You'll have a life, you'll date...

104
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:29,590
No, I won't. I'll be at the bottom of the dating barrel now.

105
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:32,260
The only guys below me will be Four-Divorce Guy...

106
00:06:32,430 --> 00:06:34,890
uh, Murderer Guy...

107
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:36,310
and geologists.

108
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:42,190
Ross, you're being ridiculous. You are cute and smart and sweet.

109
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:45,610
That is much more important than three stupid divorces.

110
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:48,820
Have you dated anyone who's been divorced three times?

111
00:06:49,030 --> 00:06:53,370
That's not fair. Most guys that have been divorced three times are 60.

112
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:57,620
Nobody cares about this except you.

113
00:06:57,830 --> 00:07:01,160
This embarrassment thing is all in your head.

114
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:04,500
- Here, I'll show you. Come here.     - What?

115
00:07:04,750 --> 00:07:08,880
Hi. My friend Ross is about to be divorced for the third time.

116
00:07:09,090 --> 00:07:10,550
But wouldn't you date him?

117
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:14,890
And if you wait right here, I'll go get Ross.

118
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:20,930
- Hey.     - Agh. Thought you were Rachel.

119
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:24,190
- What gave me away?     - I gotta tell her.

120
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:27,570
Get it over with. I told Ross and Phoebe. She's the only one left.

121
00:07:27,730 --> 00:07:30,400
It's official. We're moving in together.

122
00:07:30,650 --> 00:07:31,780
No turning back.

123
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:33,990
Are you scared? Are you?

124
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:36,240
No.

125
00:07:36,450 --> 00:07:39,330
That was my scariest voice. You're brave.

126
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:43,250
- Hey. Ugh.     - Hey.

127
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:44,580
The worst day.

128
00:07:44,830 --> 00:07:49,420
You're finally making progress at work, then your boss calls you Racquel.

129
00:07:50,630 --> 00:07:52,880
First four years of my work, they called me...

130
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:03,100
- Seriously.     - I believe you.

131
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:08,520
It was in the middle of a meeting, so no one wants to correct her.

132
00:08:08,730 --> 00:08:10,440
So everyone's calling me Racquel.

133
00:08:10,690 --> 00:08:14,400
By the end of the day, the mailroom guys were calling me Rocky.

134
00:08:16,030 --> 00:08:19,580
Well, I still think you're very, very nice and very pretty.

135
00:08:20,580 --> 00:08:21,620
What?

136
00:08:23,290 --> 00:08:24,830
All yours, babe.

137
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:27,130
Rachel, come here.

138
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:28,880
Have a seat.

139
00:08:29,590 --> 00:08:30,750
Okay.

140
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:33,300
Listen, um, Chandler and I...

141
00:08:34,010 --> 00:08:35,840
are going to live together.

142
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:37,260
Here.

143
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:41,770
Oh, my God.

144
00:08:43,270 --> 00:08:44,810
That's so great!

145
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:48,940
I'm so happy for you guys!

146
00:08:49,150 --> 00:08:50,230
Really?

147
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:52,820
And that was so sweet of you to ask.

148
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:56,910
The three of us are gonna have such a good time living together!

149
00:08:58,740 --> 00:08:59,820
Yes, we are.

150
00:09:00,950 --> 00:09:04,120
Chandler, you'll have to watch those long showers you take...

151
00:09:04,370 --> 00:09:07,290
because you know Racquel can't be late.

152
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:10,380
- Rach.     - He'll work on that.

153
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:13,800
Oh. Aw, this is so exciting!

154
00:09:14,130 --> 00:09:16,010
Oh, wow.

155
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:19,260
Come and knock on our door

156
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:23,680
We'll be waiting for you

157
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:30,940
See? Once you know the stories, it's not that bad.

158
00:09:31,150 --> 00:09:34,650
First marriage: Wife's hidden sexuality. Not my fault.

159
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:38,820
Second marriage: Said the wrong name at the altar.

160
00:09:39,070 --> 00:09:40,780
A little my fault.

161
00:09:42,030 --> 00:09:45,120
Third marriage: They shouldn't let you get married...

162
00:09:45,370 --> 00:09:47,790
when you're drunk and have writing on your face.

163
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,540
Nevada's fault.

164
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:55,050
So, what do you think, ladies? Who wouldn't want to date him?

165
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:57,760
The divorces don't bother me. I'd date him.

166
00:09:57,930 --> 00:09:59,470
But not while he's still married.

167
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:01,720
And you, wouldn't you want a date?

168
00:10:01,890 --> 00:10:03,970
I'm not dating at all anymore.

169
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:06,560
I was only dating guys that were bad for me.

170
00:10:06,730 --> 00:10:08,440
So I decided that until I work that...

171
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:10,060
Good. Good. Whatever.

172
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:12,560
What about you, Meg?

173
00:10:12,730 --> 00:10:15,480
Well, I don't care about the divorces either.

174
00:10:15,690 --> 00:10:17,820
But I wouldn't date him.

175
00:10:18,950 --> 00:10:22,740
It's just that he's obviously still in love with this Rachel girl.

176
00:10:22,910 --> 00:10:24,160
What?

177
00:10:24,330 --> 00:10:27,660
She said, "He's obviously still in love with this Rachel girl."

178
00:10:30,580 --> 00:10:33,920
This is crazy. I mean, yes, Rachel is my good friend.

179
00:10:34,170 --> 00:10:36,800
And I have loved her in the past...

180
00:10:37,050 --> 00:10:39,340
but now, she is just my wife.

181
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:43,760
Phoebe, will you help me out here?

182
00:10:43,970 --> 00:10:47,020
Well, I thought you loved her when you married her.

183
00:10:47,270 --> 00:10:51,690
We were drunk! I would've married Joey with that amount of alcohol.

184
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:55,360
Hey! You could do a lot worse than Joey Tribbiani!

185
00:10:57,900 --> 00:10:59,740
I'm sorry, but you guys are wrong.

186
00:10:59,950 --> 00:11:03,200
I just don't want to be divorced three times.

187
00:11:03,410 --> 00:11:05,870
Yes, and now he's using this three-divorces reason...

188
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:09,200
because he wants to stay married to her because he loves her.

189
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:11,870
I must say, well done. Bravo, Meg.

190
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:15,630
Okay, fine. If this is what you think...

191
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:18,130
forget about the whole three-divorce thing.

192
00:11:18,300 --> 00:11:22,590
I'll go to my lawyer's office right now and get this marriage annulled. Okay?

193
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:24,720
She means nothing to me.

194
00:11:24,890 --> 00:11:27,260
Noth... Nothing!

195
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:32,480
Okay, now I wouldn't date you because you seem a little creepy.

196
00:11:32,940 --> 00:11:35,110
I am so attracted to him right now.

197
00:11:40,490 --> 00:11:43,200
When will we tell Rachel what actually will happen?

198
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:44,450
Soon.

199
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:47,490
I just couldn't before. You saw how upset Joey got.

200
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:50,080
I couldn't do it. She's my best friend.

201
00:11:50,290 --> 00:11:51,790
Joey's my best friend.

202
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:54,580
I'm not your best friend?

203
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,250
You just said...!

204
00:11:57,420 --> 00:11:58,710
Ugh.

205
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:01,050
Of course, you're my best friend.

206
00:12:02,010 --> 00:12:03,300
Would you tell Rachel?

207
00:12:03,930 --> 00:12:06,680
- All right. At least I'm prepared.     - Okay.

208
00:12:08,390 --> 00:12:09,850
- Oh, yes.     - Hey!

209
00:12:10,020 --> 00:12:11,560
Hey, hey.

210
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:14,520
- They're not for you. Are you upset?     - I am now.

211
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:18,860
Hey, roomie.

212
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,940
Okay, bye.

213
00:12:24,490 --> 00:12:25,660
Rach. Ahem.

214
00:12:25,950 --> 00:12:29,580
There's something, um, important I have to tell you.

215
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:31,080
Are you pregnant?

216
00:12:32,290 --> 00:12:34,160
No, but I'm throwing this shirt away.

217
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,330
I think there was a little misunderstanding before.

218
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:39,630
- Mm-hm.     - Um...

219
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:44,800
When I said that, uh, Chandler and I wanted to live together...

220
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:48,260
we meant alone together.

221
00:12:52,310 --> 00:12:55,480
Oh, my God. That's funny. I can't believe I did that.

222
00:12:55,730 --> 00:12:58,400
No, sweetie. You know what? This is my fault.

223
00:12:58,650 --> 00:13:00,270
I wasn't clear.

224
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:02,530
I'm really sorry.

225
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:06,650
Listen, you take as much time as you need to move out, okay?

226
00:13:06,910 --> 00:13:08,620
There's absolutely no rush.

227
00:13:09,910 --> 00:13:12,200
Okay.

228
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:19,670
Don't you want a cookie?

229
00:13:20,590 --> 00:13:21,750
Sure.

230
00:13:24,260 --> 00:13:25,420
Thanks.

231
00:13:25,590 --> 00:13:26,930
Do you need a tissue?

232
00:13:27,090 --> 00:13:28,640
Mm-hm.

233
00:13:31,010 --> 00:13:33,560
- Where did you get these?     - I made them.

234
00:13:33,770 --> 00:13:36,480
Oh, God, they're so yummy!

235
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:43,480
It's gonna be weird when I come home and you're not here.

236
00:13:43,780 --> 00:13:45,530
No more Joey and Chan's.

237
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:47,950
No more J and C's.

238
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:51,570
Want to go to Joey and Chandler's? Can't. It's not there.

239
00:13:52,580 --> 00:13:55,950
I'll be across the hall. We can still do all the same stuff.

240
00:13:56,210 --> 00:13:58,960
We won't be able in the night and have those long talks...

241
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:01,210
about our feelings and the future.

242
00:14:02,290 --> 00:14:03,840
Not once did we do that.

243
00:14:06,050 --> 00:14:07,510
- Hi.     - Hey.

244
00:14:08,300 --> 00:14:11,430
So I told Rachel that it's just gonna be the two of us.

245
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:13,970
Oh, yeah? Well, how'd she take it?

246
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:16,350
Really well. Yeah.

247
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:18,100
Surprisingly well.

248
00:14:18,350 --> 00:14:21,560
She didn't cry. She wasn't angry or sad.

249
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:27,940
And you're upset because you didn't make your best friend cry?

250
00:14:28,700 --> 00:14:31,030
All I'm asking for is a little emotion.

251
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:33,410
Is that too much to ask after six years?

252
00:14:33,660 --> 00:14:36,410
What, are Rachel and I not as close as you guys?

253
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:40,750
I mean, did we not have as much fun? Don't I deserve a few tears?

254
00:14:42,170 --> 00:14:44,170
When we told Joey, he cried his eyes out.

255
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:48,170
Hey! I did not cry my eyes out!

256
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:50,840
Come on, it's like the end of an era.

257
00:14:51,090 --> 00:14:52,970
No more J-Man and Channy's!

258
00:14:54,970 --> 00:14:57,310
Okay, I gotta ask, who calls us that?

259
00:15:03,860 --> 00:15:06,150
You got married again?

260
00:15:07,150 --> 00:15:08,190
Yes.

261
00:15:09,110 --> 00:15:12,700
So that's your second marriage in two years?

262
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:15,160
Yes. Second in two years.

263
00:15:15,410 --> 00:15:17,740
Third, overall.

264
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:21,250
I have been a divorce attorney for 23 years...

265
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:24,580
and never have I had so much business from one client.

266
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:29,340
Why don't you tell me what happened?

267
00:15:30,260 --> 00:15:34,050
Basically, Rachel and I were in Vegas, and we got drunk.

268
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:37,600
I'm sorry, is this the same Rachel whose name you said...

269
00:15:37,850 --> 00:15:39,720
at the altar in the second marriage?

270
00:15:39,930 --> 00:15:41,770
Yes, yes, yes. Heh.

271
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:43,940
But I do not love her.

272
00:15:44,150 --> 00:15:45,230
Oh.

273
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:47,070
That's better then.

274
00:15:48,530 --> 00:15:51,990
This was just a drunken mistake, and I need to get it annulled.

275
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,320
I see.

276
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:56,410
Have you considered therapy?

277
00:15:58,330 --> 00:16:02,120
I think just the annulment for today.

278
00:16:02,410 --> 00:16:04,710
- There are some forms to fill out.     - Easy.

279
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:09,380
We'll need witnesses who can testify that you were not of sound mind.

280
00:16:09,590 --> 00:16:11,460
No problem. Heh.

281
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:14,880
We'll need you and Rachel to testify before a judge.

282
00:16:15,470 --> 00:16:16,760
Ooh.

283
00:16:18,510 --> 00:16:20,850
There's no way to do this without her?

284
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:24,980
Because I kind of already told her it was taken care of.

285
00:16:25,190 --> 00:16:27,190
Of course you did.

286
00:16:29,070 --> 00:16:33,440
Look, you can't get an annulment unless you and Rachel are both there.

287
00:16:33,650 --> 00:16:34,820
Uh-huh.

288
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:38,410
What about someone who looks like Rachel?

289
00:16:39,990 --> 00:16:41,950
I will think about the therapy.

290
00:16:47,710 --> 00:16:48,790
- Hey.     - Hey.

291
00:16:49,630 --> 00:16:54,010
So, um, I was thinking that maybe we should start dividing up our stuff.

292
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:56,090
Okay.

293
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:58,550
No point in dragging it out.

294
00:16:59,100 --> 00:17:02,220
Dragging out the long process of you moving out...

295
00:17:02,470 --> 00:17:04,600
and us not living together anymore.

296
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:06,100
Okay.

297
00:17:09,980 --> 00:17:11,440
- Hey, Rach.     - Yeah?

298
00:17:11,650 --> 00:17:14,240
What about this? Who gets this?

299
00:17:14,450 --> 00:17:18,200
I don't know if I want it because it might be too many memories.

300
00:17:19,870 --> 00:17:21,410
- What is that?     - I don't know.

301
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:24,580
Rachel.

302
00:17:24,910 --> 00:17:27,790
How about this? I want you to have the big plate.

303
00:17:28,830 --> 00:17:32,090
Wow, Monica, thanks. I love this plate.

304
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:35,210
Something to remember me by.

305
00:17:36,510 --> 00:17:39,140
Mon, you're not dying. I'm just moving out.

306
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:42,600
We're gonna see each other all the time.

307
00:17:42,890 --> 00:17:45,770
But still, it's a big change.

308
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:49,150
The end of an era, you might say.

309
00:17:52,070 --> 00:17:53,940
Are you okay? You're not blinking.

310
00:17:55,150 --> 00:17:59,320
I'm fine. I was thinking about how it's an end of an era.

311
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:01,370
Oh, all right.

312
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:07,410
But I gotta say, I don't think six years counts as an era.

313
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:10,540
An era is defined as a significant period of time.

314
00:18:10,790 --> 00:18:14,170
It was significant for me. Maybe it wasn't significant to you!

315
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:17,800
- What is the matter with you?     - What is the matter with you?

316
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:20,800
Why aren't you more upset?

317
00:18:21,050 --> 00:18:24,100
Aren't you gonna be sad that we're not living together?

318
00:18:24,350 --> 00:18:26,310
Aren't you gonna miss me at all?

319
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:29,480
Monica, all right. But don't get mad at me.

320
00:18:31,190 --> 00:18:33,820
It's just a little hard to believe.

321
00:18:34,570 --> 00:18:36,070
What's hard to believe?

322
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:40,360
I mean, it's you guys. You do this kind of stuff, you know?

323
00:18:40,610 --> 00:18:44,700
You were gonna get married in Vegas, and then you backed out.

324
00:18:44,950 --> 00:18:49,370
I'm not upset because I don't see you going through with it. I'm sorry.

325
00:18:52,920 --> 00:18:54,420
Rachel.

326
00:18:55,500 --> 00:18:57,460
It's going to happen.

327
00:18:57,840 --> 00:18:59,300
Chandler is gonna move in here.

328
00:18:59,510 --> 00:19:02,390
- But I...     - No, wait. Just let me finish, okay?

329
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:07,100
This isn't something that we just impulsively decided to do in Vegas.

330
00:19:07,350 --> 00:19:09,850
This is something that we both really want.

331
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:14,060
And it is going to happen.

332
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:16,230
It is?

333
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:19,690
Really?

334
00:19:20,150 --> 00:19:21,820
Yeah, sweetie.

335
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:27,540
You mean, we're not gonna live together anymore?

336
00:19:28,790 --> 00:19:29,870
No.

337
00:19:31,250 --> 00:19:32,290
Well...

338
00:19:33,210 --> 00:19:35,960
Oh, my God. I'm gonna miss you so much.

339
00:19:36,170 --> 00:19:37,960
I'm gonna miss you.

340
00:19:39,090 --> 00:19:40,920
I mean, it's the end of an era!

341
00:19:41,130 --> 00:19:42,630
I know!

342
00:19:46,010 --> 00:19:48,510
- Okay, bye.     - Oh, no.

343
00:19:49,220 --> 00:19:51,520
So did you get the annulment?

344
00:19:51,730 --> 00:19:54,850
- I couldn't.     - I knew it. Because you love Rachel.

345
00:19:55,650 --> 00:19:58,570
It's not that. Annulments are more complicated...

346
00:19:58,820 --> 00:20:01,070
Complicated because of the love.

347
00:20:01,530 --> 00:20:04,110
I do not love Rachel.

348
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:06,280
I'm telling her about the whole thing...

349
00:20:06,530 --> 00:20:09,370
so we can get this marriage annulled as fast as possible.

350
00:20:09,540 --> 00:20:11,950
Would I do that if I loved her?

351
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:15,120
I've never been more convinced of your love for her.

352
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:19,630
I do not have feelings for Rachel, okay?

353
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:25,180
Oh, what's wrong?

354
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:28,390
Monica and Chandler are moving in here...

355
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:31,390
and I have to move out and everything is changing.

356
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:34,810
Oh, my, come here, come here. It's okay.

357
00:20:34,980 --> 00:20:37,360
Aw, everything's gonna be okay.

358
00:20:37,520 --> 00:20:38,650
Thank you.

359
00:20:38,820 --> 00:20:40,900
Of course.

360
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:54,750
So Ross and Rachel got married.

361
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:57,540
Monica and Chandler almost got married.

362
00:20:57,920 --> 00:20:59,630
You think you and I should hook up?

363
00:21:01,710 --> 00:21:02,960
Oh, we do. Ha, ha.

364
00:21:03,130 --> 00:21:04,670
But not just yet.

365
00:21:06,050 --> 00:21:08,140
Really? Well, when?

366
00:21:09,180 --> 00:21:10,640
Okay. Um.

367
00:21:10,810 --> 00:21:14,270
Ahem, well, first Chandler and Monica will get married...

368
00:21:14,430 --> 00:21:16,600
and be filthy rich, by the way.

369
00:21:16,810 --> 00:21:18,810
- But it won't work out.     - Wow.

370
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:20,150
I know.

371
00:21:21,650 --> 00:21:24,190
Then I'm gonna marry Chandler for the money.

372
00:21:24,360 --> 00:21:27,780
And you'll marry Rachel and have the beautiful kids.

373
00:21:27,950 --> 00:21:29,320
Great.

374
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:32,490
But then we ditch those two and we get married.

375
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:35,710
We'll have Chandler's money and Rachel's kids.

376
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:39,960
Getting custody will be easy because of Rachel's drinking problem.

377
00:21:40,540 --> 00:21:42,340
Ooh, ooh, what about Ross?

378
00:21:42,550 --> 00:21:44,880
I don't want to go into the whole thing, but, um...

379
00:21:45,050 --> 00:21:47,630
we have words and I kill him.

